+
+**ep2.a.g.p1.** *(silence)* *Visual:* Rue de Lancry, late afternoon. Toi with the painting wrapped in a café tea towel under one arm. An old building, a heavy green door, an intercom with twelve names. None of them begins with L.
+
+**ep2.a.g.p2.** *Visual:* The green door opens: Mme Diallo, the baker, comes out with an empty bread basket on her hip. She studies Toi, and the tea towel, with great suspicion.
+- MME_DIALLO · A2 «C'est un tableau volé, ça ?»
+> **Note.** Mme Diallo delivers bread in the street; nobody says to whom.
+
+**ep2.a.g.p3.** *Visual:* Mme Diallo shifts the basket to her other hip and does not move from the door.
+- MME_DIALLO · A2 «Vous cherchez qui ?»
+
+**Your task.** Tell Mme Diallo who you are looking for in this building.
+
+- **(a)** *«Je cherche un peintre.»* →
+  - MME_DIALLO · A2 «Au troisième, la porte est pleine de peinture.»
+- **(b)** *«Je cherche quelqu'un. Il signe "L.".»* →
+  - MME_DIALLO · A2 «L. ? Ce n'est pas un nom, ça. C'est une lettre.»
+- **(c)** Clumsy but sincere. *«Je cherche… un ami de mon grand-mère… de ma grand-mère.»* →
+  - MME_DIALLO · A2 «Votre grand-mère ? Elle habitait le quartier ?»
+  - *(silence)* Toi does not answer. Mme Diallo looks at the tea towel, then up at the building, and holds the green door open a moment longer than she needs to.
